.TH KOBAS 1 2000-1月 "kobas.identify" "kobas.identify"
.SH NAME
kobas.identify \- Run the KOBAS style over-representation (enrichment) analysis
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIkobas.identify(\fBforeground\fR as any, 
\fBbackground\fR as any, 
\fBgmt\fR as any, 
\fBmethod\fR as string = "h", 
\fBfdr\fR as string = "BH", 
\fBcutoff\fR as integer = 5, 
\fBdatabase\fR as string = "K", 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Run the KOBAS style over-representation (enrichment) analysis
 
 Perform the over-representation analysis with the KOBAS statistical tests: the
 foreground gene list is mapped onto the given gene set collection, then the
 members of each term are compared with the background gene list by the
 hypergeometric test, the Fisher exact test, the binomial test or the chi-square
 test.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBforeground\fB \fR\- 
 the foreground gene list: a character vector of the gene ids, or the file path of
 a KOBAS \fBannotate\fR output file (the \fBquery\fR column will be used).
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBbackground\fB \fR\- 
 the background gene list: a character vector of the gene ids, or the file path of
 a KOBAS \fBannotate\fR output file. It must be a superset of the
 **foreground** for the Fisher and the chi-square test.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgmt\fB \fR\- the gene set collection: a [Background](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.HTS.GSEA.Background) model or a GMT file path.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmethod\fB \fR\- 
 the statistical test: \fBh\fR for the Fisher exact test (default, also the
 hypergeometric test), \fBb\fR for the binomial test, \fBc\fR for the chi-square test
 and \fBx\fR for the frequency list only.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBfdr\fB \fR\- 
 the multiple testing correction: \fBBH\fR (default), \fBBY\fR, \fBQVALUE\fR or \fBNone\fR.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBcutoff\fB \fR\- 
 the minimum number of the background members of a term, terms with fewer
 background members are not used in the statistical test. Default \fB5\fR.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBdatabase\fB \fR\- 
 the database label that will be written into the \fBdatabase\fR column, default \fBK\fR
 (KEGG PATHWAY).
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a \fBdataframe\fR with the term id as the row names and the columns:
 \fBname\fR, \fBdatabase\fR, \fBinput_number\fR, \fBbackground_number\fR, \fBpvalue\fR,
 \fBp_adjust\fR and \fBinput\fR (the enriched gene ids joined by \fB;\fR).
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
KOBAS
.SH FILES
.PP
gseakit.dll
.PP
